{"t": 1794112407.1607745, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nReplacing the Decimal rounding with `int(...)` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so converted totals come out 1 minor unit low (e.g. expected 1100, got 1099).\n\nSentry error: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A\n(ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit \u2014 first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3, 2201 events, suspect commit 8c2f1d0 from this PR.)\n\nFix: round half up on an exact Decimal value in `worker/rates.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal\n\n\ndef convert(amount_minor: int, rate: float) -> int:\n    exact = Decimal(amount_minor) * Decimal(str(rate))\n    return int(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```\n\nPlease revert or land the rounding fix before the next release.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
